import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"catopt-discovery — the law-discovery engine becomes a package","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"catopt-discovery — the law-discovery engine becomes a package","type":"retro","date":"2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/discovery-package.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/discovery-package.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/discovery-package.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="catopt-discovery-—-the-law-discovery-engine-becomes-a-package" tabindex="-1">catopt-discovery — the law-discovery engine becomes a package <a class="header-anchor" href="#catopt-discovery-—-the-law-discovery-engine-becomes-a-package" aria-label="Permalink to “catopt-discovery — the law-discovery engine becomes a package”">​</a></h1><p>The <code>tools/law_*.py</code> scripts had quietly become a real subsystem: a shape census, two proposal generators, a grammar enumerator, three oracles, a ranking pipeline, a sqlite evidence store, a coherence catalogue, an admission emitter, a meta-game RL prober, two corpus generators and a real-<code>nn.Module</code> intake — ~20 kLOC across 19 modules, cross-imported through <code>sys.path.insert(0, tools_dir)</code> hacks. This week the intake caught two genuine soundness bugs in shipped lowerings, which settled the question of whether this is dev tooling or a shipped engine: it is an engine, so it moved into the monorepo as a sixth workspace package, <code>packages/catopt-discovery</code> (<code>catopt_discovery</code>).</p><p>Reproduce / verify:</p><pre><code>.venv/bin/python -m catopt_discovery.pipeline --help
.venv/bin/python -m catopt_discovery.coherence
.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_law_view_oracle.py \\
    tests/test_law_pipeline_typed.py tests/test_law_serialize.py \\
    tests/test_lemma_certificates.py tests/test_intake_defects.py
</code></pre><h2 id="_1-module-map" tabindex="-1">1. Module map <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-module-map" aria-label="Permalink to “1. Module map”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>old (<code>tools/</code>)</th><th>new (<code>catopt_discovery</code>)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>law_pipeline.py</code></td><td><code>pipeline</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_shape_census.py</code></td><td><code>census</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_proposal.py</code></td><td><code>proposal</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_shape_proposal.py</code></td><td><code>shape_proposal</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>grammar_proposal.py</code></td><td><code>grammar</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_evidence.py</code></td><td><code>evidence</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_view_oracle.py</code></td><td><code>oracle</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_impact.py</code></td><td><code>impact</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_vocab.py</code></td><td><code>vocab</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_lemma_cert.py</code></td><td><code>lemma_cert</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_intake.py</code></td><td><code>intake</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_coherence.py</code></td><td><code>coherence</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_coherence2.py</code></td><td><code>coherence2</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_verifier.py</code></td><td><code>verifier</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_emit.py</code></td><td><code>emit</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_meta_game.py</code></td><td><code>meta_game</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_gap_targeted_gen.py</code></td><td><code>gap_gen</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>law_workload_gen.py</code></td><td><code>workload_gen</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>families.py</code></td><td><code>families</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Every module keeps its CLI: <code>python tools/law_X.py</code> becomes <code>python -m catopt_discovery.&lt;mod&gt;</code>. Thin <code>tools/law_*.py</code> shims were kept <strong>only</strong> for the five entry points the README/retros invoke (<code>law_pipeline</code>, <code>law_intake</code>, <code>law_shape_census</code>, <code>law_coherence</code>, <code>law_evidence</code>) — each is a <code>main()</code> re-export; everything else moved without a shim.</p><h2 id="_2-what-the-move-surfaced" tabindex="-1">2. What the move surfaced <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-what-the-move-surfaced" aria-label="Permalink to “2. What the move surfaced”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Dependencies.</strong> The package needs <code>catopt-core</code>, <code>catopt-torch</code>, <code>catopt-orchestrator</code> <em>and</em> torch — <code>impact</code> imports <code>catopt_orchestrator.optimize._lower_extracted</code> at top level, and <code>vocab</code>/<code>emit</code> reach orchestrator internals lazily. The package was declared with all four deps.</li><li><strong>The <code>bench</code> boundary.</strong> <code>impact</code>/<code>verifier</code> lazily import <code>bench.suites.correctness.law_bench.LAW_CASES</code> — <code>bench</code> is a repo-root package, not an installed distribution. The engine now reaches it through <code>catopt_discovery.REPO_ROOT</code> (derived from the editable file location), keeping the same sys.path mechanism but computed honestly.</li><li><strong>Artifacts stayed in <code>tools/</code>.</strong> <code>intake_corpus.json</code> and <code>intake_tensors.pt</code> did not move; <code>intake</code> resolves them through <code>catopt_discovery.TOOLS</code>.</li><li><strong>Staying → moved coupling.</strong> <code>lab/train/train_rl_policy.py</code> and <code>lab/train/train_search_policy.py</code> (which stay) import <code>families</code> (which moved). Their <code>import families</code> lines became <code>from catopt_discovery import families</code> — the only edits to staying files. No moved module imports a stayed one.</li><li><strong>ty debt.</strong> <code>tools/</code> was never type-checked; moving the code under <code>packages/</code> put it under <code>ty</code>, which reported 35 diagnostics — all fixed with real annotations/guards (a wrongly-typed <code>CorpusStats</code> field, <code>Op|Var</code> unions, <code>dict[str, Any]</code> kwargs bags, one <code>contextlib.suppress</code> replacing <code>except: pass</code>, and a <code>Callable</code>-hop for the verifier monkeypatch). Zero <code>exclude</code>/<code># ty: ignore</code>.</li><li><strong>bandit.</strong> <code>packages/</code> is SAST-scanned; the moved code tripped six <code>B101</code> asserts and one <code>B110</code> try/except/pass. All fixed in code (explicit raises / <code>cast</code> / <code>suppress</code>) — no config widening.</li><li><strong>radon.</strong> The baseline only covered <code>packages/</code>; the move brought ~800 previously-unratcheted functions under the gate. The baseline was regenerated (<code>--update</code>), pinning their current complexity — per the ratchet convention, not as an exception.</li></ul><h2 id="_3-config-edits" tabindex="-1">3. Config edits <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-config-edits" aria-label="Permalink to “3. Config edits”">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>pyproject.toml</code>: <code>catopt-discovery</code> added to <code>[project]</code> dependencies and <code>[tool.uv.sources]</code>; <code>packages/*</code> workspace glob picks the member up automatically.</li><li><code>[tool.ty.environment]</code>: <code>packages/catopt-discovery/src</code> added to <code>extra-paths</code>.</li><li><code>[tool.importlinter]</code>: <code>catopt_discovery</code> added to <code>root_packages</code>, to the core <code>forbidden</code> contract, and as the top <code>dependency layers</code> layer (it reads core/torch/orchestrator; nothing may depend back).</li><li><code>scripts/complexity_baseline.json</code>: regenerated (+797 entries).</li><li>Coverage <strong>not</strong> extended: <code>catopt_discovery</code> is not in <code>[tool.coverage.run] source</code> — the 100% floor is a separate staged effort (the engine is mostly CLI/reporting code; its test coverage is the law-focused subset, not the whole surface).</li><li><code>scripts/runtime_types.sh</code> and <code>scripts/mutmut.sh</code> keep their hardcoded package lists — discovery is deliberately not instrumented there yet, same staging decision as coverage.</li></ul><h2 id="_4-what-did-not-change" tabindex="-1">4. What did not change <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-what-did-not-change" aria-label="Permalink to “4. What did not change”">​</a></h2><ul><li>The five shimmed CLIs still work as <code>python tools/law_X.py</code>.</li><li><code>tools/</code> keeps its dev-infra (<code>radon_ratchet.py</code>, <code>mutmut.sh</code>, <code>runtime_types.sh</code>, <code>complexity_baseline.json</code>), the bench/RL drivers (<code>contraction_*.py</code>, <code>train_*.py</code>, <code>calibrate_profile.py</code>, <code>executor_cost_probe.py</code>, <code>coordination_probe.py</code>, <code>law_wallclock.py</code>) and the artifacts (<code>evidence.db</code>, <code>intake_corpus.json</code>, <code>intake_tensors.pt</code>).</li><li><code>evidence.code_rev</code>&#39;s <code>_CODE_PATHS</code> already covered <code>packages</code> + <code>tools</code>, so verdict cache keys still capture the engine&#39;s code — no schema or key change.</li></ul><h2 id="_5-gates-after-the-move" tabindex="-1">5. Gates after the move <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-gates-after-the-move" aria-label="Permalink to “5. Gates after the move”">​</a></h2><p><code>ruff check</code> / <code>ruff format --check</code> clean on <code>packages</code> + <code>tools</code>; <code>ty check</code> 0 errors; <code>vulture</code> clean; <code>lint-imports</code> 4/4 contracts kept; <code>bandit</code> 0 findings; <code>semgrep</code> (offline config) 0 findings; <code>radon_ratchet</code> ok (2866 functions); the five focused law test files pass (82 tests). Full <code>pytest</code> and coverage runs were not part of this change&#39;s verification (a background coverage run was in progress; the suite exercises <code>catopt_discovery</code> transitively through the focused tests).</p>`,15)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};